# X0B (PRE): status, rescan, quad reset, then build the shipping image tp4-serve-10 with c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix baked as the image default serving profile and
# THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked as that profile's max-num-seqs (8), as SB8 did. READ: the provenance report '(c) the image default is the BAKED profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix',
# no problem line, 'baking the serving default c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix with a session cap of 8', the evidence files named in the build log at their pinned sha256, the image id.
# The build exits early if the tag exists (a changed commit needs a new tag). Real time 4 min (status+rescan+reset) + 22 min build.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the ship/262k-prefix pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over that file on a throwaway
# commit of ship/262k-prefix (with its evidence files committed) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has
# the order, stop rules, real minutes, NEEDS and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10 is the ONE shipping image X0B builds: every job serves it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status rescan reset build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix
